<rml>
<head>
	<title>compare</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<style>
		/*
			The two text engines against each other, in one window.

			The top half is live: fields resolved by the shader every frame, so it re-resolves at
			whatever size the window is. The bottom half is a picture of the same document
			rendered by the old FreeType engine, scaled by the same ratio.

			Open it with --dp-reference matching the window height and the two sit at 1:1, where
			the comparison is fair: same font file, same sizes, same ground. Resize from there and
			they stop being comparable, which is the other half of the point - one is re-resolved
			and the other is magnified.
		*/
		body
		{
			font-family: "Inter 18pt";
			color: #e8e8f0;
			background-color: #16161c;
			padding: 12dp;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			box-sizing: border-box;
		}

		div { display: block; }

		.label
		{
			font-size: 12dp;
			color: #f0c674;
			margin-bottom: 6dp;
		}

		.note { font-size: 12dp; color: #6a6a7a; margin-bottom: 14dp; }

		.line { margin-bottom: 6dp; }
		.s10 { font-size: 10dp; }
		.s13 { font-size: 13dp; }
		.s16 { font-size: 16dp; }
		.s20 { font-size: 20dp; }
		.s28 { font-size: 28dp; }

		/* Sized in dp so the picture scales with the window exactly as the live text does. */
		.reference
		{
			display: block;
			width: 620dp;
			height: 170dp;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="label">Distance fields, live</div>

	<div class="line s10">Handgloves 10 — illiminating quick brown foxes</div>
	<div class="line s13">Handgloves 13 — illiminating quick brown foxes</div>
	<div class="line s16">Handgloves 16 — illiminating quick brown foxes</div>
	<div class="line s20">Handgloves 20 — illiminating quick brown foxes</div>
	<div class="line s28">Handgloves 28 — illiminating quick</div>

	<div class="label">FreeType raster, a picture of the same document</div>
	<div class="note">Sharp only at the default window size. Everything past that is magnification.</div>

	<img class="reference" src="freetype_reference.png"/>
</body>
</rml>
